WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:04.980
A star-studded cast featuring Oscar winners&nbsp;
and icons, and an unusual premise dreamed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:09.300
up by two unlikely collaborators. Here's what&nbsp;
you need to know about Peacock's "Poker Face."

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:13.980
Natasha Lyonne is probably best known for&nbsp;
playing the brash and combative Nicky Nichols&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:18.300
on Netflix megahit "Orange is the New Black."&nbsp;
More recently, Lyonne received recognition&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:22.740
for performance on Netflix's "Russian Doll,"&nbsp;
which she also co-created. The second season&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:27.240
of "Russian Doll" hit the streaming service&nbsp;
in April 2022, and Lyonne has hinted that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:30.900
she'd like to wrap up the series in a third&nbsp;
season. While it's unclear whether or not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:35.100
Netflix will renew the popular show, the New&nbsp;
York native already has her next role booked.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:39.180
"Poker Face" is described as a&nbsp;
mystery-comedy-drama. Lyonne is set&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:43.500
to play Charlie Cale, a person with a knack for&nbsp;
deducing when someone isn't telling the truth.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:48.480
As noted in a joint statement from Lyonne and&nbsp;
"Poker Face" creator Rian Johnson, via Deadline,

00:01:02.601 --> 00:01:06.141
"Hello Miss Cale. I'm happy to finally meet you."

00:01:06.141 --> 00:01:09.840
Lyonne and Johnson also clued potential&nbsp;
viewers into the show's genesis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:13.740
giving credit to a dinner conversation they&nbsp;
once shared. As their statement explained,

00:01:31.101 --> 00:01:35.280
According to Deadline, the first season of&nbsp;
"Poker Face" will consist of 10 episodes. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:40.740
first four episodes will premiere on January&nbsp;
26, 2023, with subsequent chapters following&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:45.840
each week on Thursdays. In an interview on "Late&nbsp;
Night with Seth Meyers," Lyonne commented on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:49.740
difference between Netflix and broadcast&nbsp;
releases. Referring to "Orange is the New&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:53.935
Black," Lyonne discussed how quickly viewers&nbsp;
devoured shows that were dropped all at once.

00:01:53.935 --> 00:01:58.200
"It's a 13-hour show. They consume it in&nbsp;
under 30 minutes flat. I don't know how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:01.440
they do it. That's where I learned&nbsp;
about the space-time continuum."

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:05.760
Instead, Peacock's weekly release schedule will&nbsp;
hopefully have impatient fans on the edge of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:09.660
their seats waiting for new installments. It&nbsp;
will also leave Lyonne's brain free to craft&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:13.680
new stories and not worry about the vagaries of&nbsp;
the universe and other metaphysical mysteries.

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:18.180
A slate of guest stars with familiar faces&nbsp;
are set to appear alongside Natasha Lyonne in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:22.980
"Poker Face." According to Deadline, "Get Out"&nbsp;
star Lil Rel Howery will play a local sheriff,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:27.240
and he'll be joined by "The Good Place" star&nbsp;
Jameela Jamil, Hollywood legends Ellen Barkin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:30.720
and Nick Nolte, and "500 Hundred Days&nbsp;
of Summer" actor Joseph Gordon-Levitt.

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:35.700
Joining the already incredible cast is Lyonne's&nbsp;
"Orange Is the New Black" co-star Dascha Polanco,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:41.400
Oscar winner Adrien Brody, "Miss Congeniality"&nbsp;
actor Benjamin Bratt, "Succession" star Cherry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:45.300
Jones, filmmaker and fashion designer&nbsp;
Chloë Sevigny, former teen icon turned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:50.760
director Clea DuVall, star of "Wednesday" Luis&nbsp;
Guzmán, and the original Hellboy, Ron Perlman.

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:54.360
"Knives Out" director Rian Johnson&nbsp;
will direct, write, and co-executive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:58.860
produce "Poker Face" along with his frequent&nbsp;
collaborator Ram Bergman and Natasha Lyonne,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:04.605
per Deadline. Lyonne and Johnson recently met at a&nbsp;
party and instantly clicked. She told Vanity Fair,

00:03:12.801 --> 00:03:14.940
In a statement via TheWrap, Johnson said,

00:03:26.095 --> 00:03:28.500
Lisa Katz, NBCUniversal Television and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:31.200
Streaming's president of scripted&nbsp;
content, said in a statement,

00:03:44.577 --> 00:03:48.657
Johnson and Lyonne will be joined as&nbsp;
co-executive producers by Maya Rudolph.

